(Battambang): On April 19, 2023, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, inspected the actual situation at the International Coconut Gate in Kamrieng District, where the workers were returning to Thailand after visiting their hometown. On the occasion of Khmer New Year.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Sok Lou further advised the officers and authorities stationed at the International Coconut Gate to make every effort to facilitate the entry and exit of workers back to work legally and expedite Filling out cross-border forms for citizens and workers as soon as possible, including avoiding taking unofficial fees from citizens and workers traveling to and from this international gate.
The Battambang Provincial Governor's direct inspection at the International Coconut Gate was made after receiving information on social media that there was money being taken from the workers and people who came in and out of this international gate.
According to a report from the Immigration Police at the International Coconut Port, the criticism on Facebook was misleading. In fact, the Cambodians paid more than 1,000 baht per person because the Thai side rented a car to transport them to various destinations in Thailand, not to take money from the border officials. .
