In response, Mr. Youk Chhang asked the Ambassador to provide details on the Russian skills that died in Kampong Cham province so that the Documentation Center of Cambodia could conduct further research and share history with students. Youk Chhang also invited the Ambassador of the Russian Federation to visit the Kampong Cham Provincial Documentation Center and the site where the seven Russian experts died in 1983.
In discussions with Mr. Youk Chhang, Ambassador Anatoly Borovic supported the work of the Documentation Center of Cambodia in compiling and teaching the history of Democratic Kampuchea to prevent it from happening again.
Mr. Anatoly also expressed his satisfaction with the interviews and medical examinations of Khmer Rouge survivors throughout Cambodia, which helped them.
