The ceremony was accompanied by the District Governor, together with the members of the Provincial Committee of the Red Cross Branch, Branch Director, District Authority, and brought some food and other materials to 36 more families affected by the typhoon in 3 communes, including: Koh Sneng commune, Preah Rumkel commune, Osvay commune, Borey Osvay Sen Chey district.
On that occasion, Mr. Svay Sam Eang sent a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always pays attention to the well-being of all people who are suffering, especially the disabled, the elderly and natural disasters. Irrespective of caste, color, creed, religion, or political affiliation.
Donation of the Cambodian Red Cross and the direct budget of the Governor distributed to 36 families affected by the typhoon, each received 50,000 Riels, including 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 box of fish, 1 lot of water and materials. Some uses.
General Hun Manet Distributes Relief to 26 Families of Retired and Disabled Soldiers in Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): Major General Chhun Mao, Deputy Commander of the 5th Military Zone and Commander of the 1st Direction, Banteay Meanchey, this morning, April 18, 2023, met and handed over the gifts of General Hun Manet and Mrs. Pich Chanmony to the soldiers. Retired 26 families of disabled soldiers.
On that occasion, Major General Chhun Mao emphasized that retired soldiers and disabled soldiers have great benefits to the nation and the people. He added that even though Uncle Puming and his siblings have completed their defense roles and responsibilities, this great merit has left an indelible mark on the next generation.
Major General Chhun Mao conveyed greetings from General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army and Mrs. Pich Chanmony to retired and disabled soldiers.
Lt. Gen. Chhun Mao added that the Commander of the Army and Mrs. always take into account the well-being and livelihood of our veterans, because the veterans are the ones who have the merits of the motherland and the people. Contribute with Samdech Techo Hun Sen to implement a win-win policy to make our country peaceful and fully united as it is today.
