Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department Disseminates Minimum Standards for Private Health Centers to Nearly 400 Private Health Professionals
(Tbong Khmum): Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department In the afternoon of April 18, 2023, Dr. Sok Srun, Advisor of the Ministry of Health and Director of the Hospital Department of the Ministry of Health, held a meeting to disseminate the minimum standards for private health facilities to teachers. Doctors at Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department.
The event was attended by Dr. Chhorn Mony, Deputy Director of Provincial Health Department, Pharmacist Phol Ponleu, Deputy Director of Provincial Health Department, Office around the Department, Chiefs of the 7 Executive Offices, Municipalities / Districts, Professions, Doctors, Nurses and Mr. Nearly 400 private health professionals across Tbong Khmum province.
Pharmacist Phol Ponleu read out the report on the activities of Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department in the past to monitor and take strict action against health service providers and owners of private health care facilities in the province to the ceremony. .
On this occasion, Dr. Sok Srun said that the meeting was held to strengthen the provision of health services in private health facilities in accordance with the law and professional ethics with a high sense of responsibility.
The doctor pointed out that the minimum standard for private health facilities can really help strengthen private health services, because this minimum standard sets the appropriate conditions for the opening of quality control during operation and the renewal of the local owner. Private health care must be followed as necessary and always.
