Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan: The success of Samdech Techo's win-win policy has made Cambodia move forward firmly on the path of peace, national unity, racial and religious harmony.
(Banteay Meanchey): Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Banteay Meanchey Province, stated that the success of the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has made Cambodia step forward. Strong face on the path of peace, national unification, national and religious harmony.
This statement was made by Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan on the occasion that he presided over a meeting with Muslims to discuss vegetarianism and solidarity dinner on the evening of April 18, 2023.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan paid a courtesy call on the top leaders of the nation and expressed his deep gratitude and love to all Cambodian Muslims who have always provided credible support to the royal leadership. The Cambodian government led by the Cambodian People's Party in all circumstances to continue to build and develop the country.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, the success of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy, also paid homage to the rights and freedoms of the faith, promoted and supported all religions and ethnic groups, and strongly opposed discrimination, dividing religious beliefs in order to transform all religious potential into A strong national unity force in safeguarding peace, national unity and promoting socio-economic development.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by the Cambodian People's Party, has given senior positions to the leaders of the Khmer Muslim community at the national and sub-national levels.
