Minister Vong Soth Meets National Council for Social Protection to gather input to prepare for a long-term vision on social protection in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, received Dr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State and Secretary General of the National Council for Social Protection, to discuss the work and gather input to prepare for a long-term vision on social protection. In Cambodia.
Permission for the National Council for Social Protection to meet and discuss on April 18, 2023.
Mr. Vong Soth thanked and highly appreciated the National Council for Social Protection, chaired by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, for his active efforts to make the social protection system more progressive. Whatever the circumstances.
The Minister said that the Ministry of Social Affairs will continue to cooperate to provide the necessary inputs to make the second phase of the National Social Protection Policy Framework comprehensive and relevant to the national social assistance programs that the Ministry is implementing.
Dr. John Narith stated that the development of social protection system is an important factor to achieve equitable economic growth and environment based on political stability, macroeconomic and progress in socio-economic development, the Royal Government of Cambodia. National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025, which has helped to improve the income security of the people through the effective implementation of the National Social Assistance Program and the Social Security Regime.
