Royal Group of Kith Meng and Prudential Cambodia Sign a Memorandum of Understanding on Strategic Business Partnership
(Singapore): Royal Group and Prudential Cambodia have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on a formal strategic business partnership, a joint venture between several projects and initiatives in Cambodia.
"Digital technology is changing the world and stakeholders are looking for strategic partnerships to increase supply and provide better system solutions to customers," said Kith Meng, President of Royal Group.
Sanjay Chakrabarty, CEO of Prudential Cambodia, said: “The strategic business partnership between Prudential Cambodia and the Royal Group demonstrates our strong commitment to bringing financial and health protection. "Affordable to every family and community in Cambodia."
The signing of the MoU is an important event in the Kingdom of Cambodia, which also links Prudential, a major life insurance company in the market, with Royal Group, an enterprise. Diversified and largest agency network to achieve a common goal of providing financial services to all regions in Cambodia.
Overall, this strategic partnership covers areas for development in Cambodia, such as insurance, banking, finance, real estate and other projects that benefit society.
Details of the strategic plan will be released later as the two companies study the potential of the joint venture.
