(Prey Veng): Police Inspectorate of Ba Phnom District, Prey Veng Province cracked down on illegal gambling (cockfighting) at Krous village, Chheu Kach commune, but during the crackdown, gamblers clashed with police, causing gunfire. One was injured.
According to the report of Prey Veng Provincial Police, which was received by Fresh News on April 18, 2023, on April 15, 2023, the police patrolled the area of Ba Phnom district to protect the security and order of the people. Citizens on the occasion of the Khmer New Year and the prevention and suppression of all kinds of crimes with 4 forces led by Lieutenant Colonel Seang Bunnal, Deputy Inspector of Ba Phnom District.
During the patrol in the above area, some people reported that there was a point of gambling (cockfighting) at Krous village, Chheu Karch commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province.
Meanwhile, the Deputy Inspector shouted and pulled out a handgun to threaten them to stop, but they refused to listen, and the Deputy Inspector went to arrest 36-year-old San Vicheka in Krous village, Chheu Karch commune, Ba Phnom district. While riding a spare motorcycle, there was a fight that caused the Deputy Inspector and San Vicheka, including the motorcycle to fall, causing a gun to explode, injuring San Vicheka, injuring his left waist.
Currently, the Deputy Inspector who caused the explosion and injuring the gambler has been placed under the supervision of the Prey Veng Provincial Police. At the same time, the provincial police commissioner also sent professional officers to inspect and research in detail to find out the clarity of this case carefully.
