Experts and real estate developers applaud the decision to postpone the implementation of package tax payments in stages until the end of 2024
(Phnom Penh): Real estate experts are pleased that the Royal Government has decided to extend the implementation of the package tax payment in stages until the end of 2024 and increase the period of package tax payment up to 18 months for small projects and Up to 36 months for large projects, this factor greatly eases the difficulties for Borey project developers and makes it more affordable for buyers to buy a home.
On April 17, 2023, the Royal Government has introduced measures to support the development of the construction and real estate sector in Borey by deciding to extend the implementation of the package tax payment in stages until the end of 2024 for housing developers. Borey, which has been operating a housing development project with a real estate business license provided by a real estate regulator and a mortgage.
Separately, companies that have been operating housing development projects in Borey without a real estate business license must hurry to register their projects to obtain a real estate business license in accordance with the procedures in force from the real estate business regulator and mortgage by the end of 2023 to receive. Continued tax payment as a package until the end of 2024.
At the same time, the Royal Government also decided to increase the period of package tax payment from 12 months to 18 months for housing developers in Borey who pay less than 1 million US dollars and from 24 months to 36 months for developers. Housing is a city that pays more than 1 million US dollars in taxes.
He explained that "the payment of package tax means that the government before approving the construction of any project, the owner of the city always study with the tax on whether the development of his project to be sold at such a price, he built at such a cost. This is how much tax to pay to the tax side. So paying taxes in this package means, like Mao, how much a tax project costs. ”
Oknha Dr. Kim Heang, President of KW Cambodia and also a Borey developer, said that this is a measure that the Royal Government has put in place in a timely manner and facilitated housing developers in difficult situations while both sellers and buyers are facing Problems with financial flow obstruction.
He added that the measures now put in place help both developers to pay taxes and home buyers to have more access to housing.
He noted that at present, most housing projects are taxed in excess of $ 1 million because they are large projects. When the state allows the tax to be paid for up to 36 months, the project owner is more likely to pay in small installments each month.
