Editorial: April 1975 and April 2023 are as different as the hell and paradise of the Cambodian national journey.
(Phnom Penh): April 1975 is a bitter note in the history of Cambodia. The events of April 1975 are now 48 years old, but many historical slogans this month have not been erased or erased from the memory of the Cambodian people who went through them.
In April 1975, two major events were noted, including the fall of Lon Nol's US-backed Khmer Republic and the victory of the Khmer Rouge on April 17. 1975 After five years of war.
In fact, during the recent traditional New Year celebrations through Angkor Sankranti in Siem Reap, as well as Sankranti events in other provinces, it was observed that Cambodians met Family and fun.
On April 17, 2023, the main national roads into Phnom Penh were crowded with vehicles, Cambodians are rushing back to Phnom Penh to continue the normal operation of business, livelihood, study and so on. After meeting relatives and friends and enjoying the Khmer New Year for the past 3 days.
From the scene on April 17, 48 years ago and April 17, 2023, it shows the stark difference of Cambodian society, which is like hell, hell and the paradise of the life of the Cambodian people.
This view is a mirror of the leading politics of the previous generation of Cambodian politicians and the current Cambodian politicians.
