In addition, the Royal Government has encouraged and requested the banking and financial institutions to facilitate the reorganization of loans to Chea Borey housing development companies based on the voluntary principles of both partners.
This decision was confirmed by a press release from the Economic and Financial Policy Committee, obtained by Fresh News this morning, April 17, 2023.
"In order to maintain the employment sustainability of the workers and to improve the ability of low- and middle-income people to be able to afford affordable housing, the Royal Government has decided to take further measures," the statement said. "Exemption from stamp duty on the transfer of ownership or possession of all types of housing in the form of a Borey with a value of less than or equal to 70,000 US dollars until the end of 2024."
"In order to maintain the stability of the construction and real estate sectors, which are considered a priority sector in supporting economic growth, the Royal Government continues to encourage and request the banking and financial institutions to restructure their loans as much as possible. Establishment based on the principle of volunteering and agreement between the institution and the housing development company Chea Borey.
Please be informed that in 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced a stamp duty exemption for home buyers worth $ 70,000 or less for one year until the end of 2022, but now Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to extend the favor. Until the end of 2024.
