During the meeting, the two sides expressed their pride in the steady development of cooperation between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) and the Vietnam Border Guard Command, which has achieved many fruitful achievements since 2004.
In particular, this good cooperation has reached another level, the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation between the two units on February 3, 2021. In the past, this Memorandum It has really played an important role in further strengthening and enhancing the effectiveness of cooperation in border management and protection to ensure security, peace, friendship, stability, cooperation and development.
In fact, the relationship between the Second Office of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Security Information Research Commission of the Border Guard Command of the Ministry of Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam has led to the establishment of a permanent mechanism to promote cooperation at the professional level through Jointly signed the Terms of Cooperation (ToR) between the two entities today as well.
The results of this work have really contributed to the strengthening of ties between the two countries and peoples, as well as the maintenance of peace, stability, public order and security along the border, which is conducive to change. Trade, tourism and peaceful living of the people on both sides in line with the motto of "good neighborliness, traditional friendship, comprehensive cooperation and long-term stability."
For the 2023 target, the two sides agreed to continue joint efforts to carry out tasks in accordance with the content of the 2019 Joint Statement between the two countries, the Protocol on Bilateral Defense Cooperation 2020-2024 and the Cooperation Plan. Annual operation 2023 between the Ministries of Defense of the two countries.
