This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen closed the meeting of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports
(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday afternoon, April 12, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. The ceremony was held at the conference hall of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
The following are the main achievements of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in the academic year 2021-2022:
As of the 2022-2023 school year, there are 18,830 public kindergartens and general education institutions, both public, community and private, of which 8,607 kindergartens, 8,067 primary schools, 1,340 secondary schools and High school 816 schools.
There are 19 technical and vocational education institutions with a total of 3,259 students, 35.6% of whom are female, and 132 higher education institutions nationwide, of which 48 are public and 84 are private, located in 20 provincial capitals. A total of 205,636 students are studying in higher education, 47.5 percent are female.
2: Youth Development
The Ministry has expanded the structure of the Youth Development Council to 33 ministries, institutions and 25 provincial capitals as a support mechanism and a roadmap to mobilize the participation of all stakeholders and focus on youth development.
The Ministry has researched and published the "Index of Cambodian Youth Development", the "Report on the Analysis of the Situation of Cambodian Youth" and established a youth management information system and smartphone app called "Youth Health" as a basis for receiving information. About the needs of youth in ministries, national and sub-national institutions, development partners, civil society organizations, the private sector and all stakeholders.
The Ministry has amended the Charter and Internal Rules of the Cambodian National Scouts through the organization of the General Assembly of the Cambodian National Scouts and the National Strategic Plan of the Cambodian National Scouts 2023-2027.
The Ministry has trained 48,567 young people in 21st century skills, 49% of whom are women, with the aim of providing at least one life-long skill to young people.
3: Physical education and sports
The Ministry has successfully organized the 3rd National Sports Competition and the 1st National Sports Competition for the Disabled. The Ministry has co-organized international sports competitions in the country, and Cambodia has won three gold, three silver and 13 bronze medals. The Ministry sent athletes to participate in international sports competitions abroad in 45 sports and won 1,370 medals, including 326 gold medals, 363 silver medals and 681 bronze medals.
For the World Championships, Cambodia won 39 gold, 52 silver, and 65 bronze medals. At the Asian Championships, Cambodia won 77 gold, 77 silver and 127 bronze medals.
