Xi Jinping: China's military needs to intensify training focused on combat situation
BEIJING: Chinese state media CCTV reported on Wednesday that Chinese President Xi Jinping has called on China's armed forces to intensify military exercises focused on the actual combat situation. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, April 12, 2023.
According to CCTV, Xi made the remarks during a visit to the Chinese navy on Tuesday. At the time, the Chinese president also added that the military must firmly defend China's sovereignty, territorial integrity and maritime interests.
Earlier this week, the Chinese military just concluded a three-day large-scale military exercise aimed at Taiwan. Tensions have risen sharply in the region following Beijing's military build-up, which considers Taiwan an inseparable part of Chinese territory. China launched the military exercise in response to a meeting between Taiwanese leaders and the speaker of the US House of Representatives in California last week.
Ukrainian Deputy Foreign Minister concludes visit to India with request for humanitarian aid and diplomatic support
NEW DELHI: Ukraine's Deputy Foreign Minister on Wednesday wrapped up a four-day visit to India after calling for humanitarian aid, including diplomatic support from New Delhi, which has so far continued to avoid condemnation. Russian invasion of Ukraine. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, April 12, 2023.
India's long-standing security ties with Russia have put New Delhi in a difficult position, and while India has called for an end to all hostilities in Ukraine, India has not directly condemned the aggression. India, meanwhile, is stepping up its purchases of discounted oil from Russia, despite Western pressure to cut off Moscow's revenue.
