Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of closing the meeting of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports
(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday afternoon, April 12, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. The ceremony was held at the conference hall of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
Please be reminded that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports held a meeting to review the work of the old year 2021-2022 and raise the work direction of the new year 2022-2023 on the morning of April 10, 2023. This year's conference of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports is held under the theme "Revolution of Education".
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the achievements are really reflected in the efforts and close cooperation of leaders, educators at all levels, teachers, parents, communities and local authorities in the development of education. To progress in accordance with their respective roles and responsibilities with a high sense of responsibility.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen highly appreciates the development partners of national and international organizations and relevant institutions who have cooperated and provided material, financial and technical support.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen, I would like to support the reform program, measures and priorities set out by the conference based on current achievements and new opportunities, and to set clear and realistic reform directions with specific goals. As well as having a clear leadership structure and implementation mechanism to build human capital with potential knowledge, skills and attitudes for the development of the nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends 6 points for further implementation to the Ministry of Education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommended to continue to strengthen and develop the education system to be stronger, more proactive, modern and responsive to the national and international environment. With this, ensuring effective and quality education services with an equitable environment, as well as promoting lifelong learning opportunities for all, especially to strive for more effective measures to improve student learning outcomes in All levels.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends to continue to develop the capacity of institutions and education officials to be full, lively and interconnected by ensuring the effectiveness of leadership and management of education officials at all levels, including reform Teacher training institutions, improving the efficiency of financing, cooperation, policy development and education planning and regular professional development for education staff and teachers.
