From January to March 2023, exports to international markets reached $ 5.3 billion, down 5.7% from the same period in 2022, according to the data. $ 5.7 billion. At the same time, Cambodia imported goods from international markets worth more than 5.9 billion US dollars, down 21.3% compared to the same period in 2022 worth 7.4 billion US dollars.
In the first three months of this year, Cambodia achieved a trade volume with international markets worth more than $ 11 billion, down 14.5%.
According to data from the General Department of Customs and Excise, garments were exported worth $ 1.6 billion, machinery, electrical appliances and accessories were valued at $ 736 million, footwear was valued at $ 323 million, rubber Exports $ 168 million, including other goods.
Pen Sovicheat, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, said recently that exports fell earlier this year due to the season to export. In fact, Cambodia, an exporter of clothing, footwear, bicycles, etc., needs to comply with the orders required to export in a given month. At the same time, agricultural products at the beginning of this year have not yet been harvested and can be exported a lot.
